n\n\nThe wavefunction (`wfc1.hdf5`), charge density (`charge-density.hdf5`), and PAW data (`paw.txt`) files are confirmed to exist from the previous step. `startingwfc = 'file'` and `startingpot = 'file'` parameters will ensure that these are used as the initial guess for the SCF cycle in Step 301. These data are critical for ensuring the Nosé-Hoover thermostat's state is preserved.\n\n\nThe Quantum ESPRESSO output (`espresso_all_steps.pwo`) contains the full simulation data from Step 0 to Step 300, which can be quickly replayed within LAMMPS. This allows for a seamless transition from the cached data to a live Quantum ESPRESSO calculation, ensuring that the Nosé-Hoover thermostat's state is perfectly preserved, thus allowing the run to continue through Step 600 without any loss of accuracy. A LAMMPS binary restart file will also be generated at the end of Step 600.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
